  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Qadreen: Generating temporary employment opportunities for the most vulnerable</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribute to mitigating the social consequences of the Syrian crisis and the economic crisis on the most vulnerable groups in the Minieh -Donnieh district.  Improve access to income and better infrastructure and public services for vulnerable refugees and Lebanese in Minieh -Donnieh district, reducing social tensions.  The present project revolves around the following theory of change:    If vulnerable men and women have access to opportunities for temporary employment in productive public infrastructure and environmental protection in the municipalities of  Bqarsouna and Bqaa Sifrine (R1) , and community -based services are provided at municipal level in Bqarsouna and Bqaa Sifrine (R2) and integrated municipal solid waste management  services are improved in Bqaa Sifrine  to reduce social tensions (R3), then access to income and better infrastructure and public services for refugees and vulnerable Lebanese in Minieh -Donnieh district will be increased, reducing social tensions.</narrative>
  </description>
